Doenet-Sync-Version: 0.7.28
Doenet-Sync-NumVariants: 1
Doenet-Sync-Hash: 15958adefcdcce74
-->
<problem>

<setup>
<selectFromSequence name="a" exclude="0" numToSelect="3" withReplacement="true" from="-10" to="10" excludecombinations="(1 1) (1 -1) (-1 1) (-1 -1)" />
<selectFromSequence name="c" exclude="0" from="-10" to="10" />

<selectFromSequence name="n" from="1" to="4" />
<select name="x">x y z</select>

<math name="factored_quadratic" simplify="full">($x+$a[1])($x+$a[2])</math>
<math name="expanded_quadratic" simplify="full" expand="true">$factored_quadratic</math>
<convertSetToList name="zero_list" simplify="full"><math>{-$a[1],-$a[2],0}</math></convertSetToList>
<math name="factor1" simplify="full">$x+$a[1]</math>
<math name="factor2" simplify="full">$x+$a[2]</math>
<math name="minus_a" simplify="full">-$a[1]</math>
<math name="minus_b" simplify="full">-$a[2]</math>
<math name="monomial" simplify="full">$c*$x^$n</math>
<math name="monomial_times_expanded_quadratic" simplify="full">$monomial*$expanded_quadratic</math>
<math name="monomial_times_factored_quadratic" simplify="full">$monomial*$factored_quadratic</math>
</setup>

Solve the equation <m>$monomial_times_expanded_quadratic =0</m> by factoring.

<p>How many solutions are there? <mathInput name="user_num_sol" /></p>

<p>The solutions are:</p>

<repeatForSequence length="min(10,$user_num_sol)" name="xs">
    <p><m>$x =</m> <mathInput /></p>
  </repeatForSequence>

<answer>
  <award>
    <when matchpartial="true">
      <mathList>
        <setup><collect componentType="mathInput" from="$xs" isResponse="true" name="collect_list" /></setup><mathList name="list" extend="$collect_list.value" />
      </mathList>
      =
      $zero_list
    </when>
  </award>

</answer>


<solution>
Factoring the quadratic <m>$expanded_quadratic</m>, we obtain <m>$factored_quadratic</m>.  Therefore, the solutions to 
<me>$monomial_times_expanded_quadratic =0</me>
are the same as the solutions to
<me>$monomial_times_factored_quadratic=0.</me>
For this factored expression to be zero, one of the factors must be zero.  
<conditionalContent>
  <case condition="$a[1]=$a[2]">
Either <m>$x=0</m> or <m>$factor1=0</m>.  Therefore there are two solutions: <m>$x=0</m> and <m>$x = $minus_a</m>.
  </case>
  <else>
Either <m>$x=0</m>, <m>$factor1=0</m>, or <m>$factor2=0</m>.  Therefore, there are three solutions: <m>$x=0</m>,  <m>$x=$minus_a</m>, and <m>$x=$minus_b</m>.
  </else>
</conditionalContent>

</solution>

</problem>